00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:09,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:10,115 --> 00:00:11,116
[grunting]

2
00:00:11,199 --> 00:00:14,703
[Kihyun] <i>When they hit you, you take it.</i>
<i>When they tell you to kneel, you kneel.</i>

3
00:00:14,786 --> 00:00:17,456
<i>The weak get crushed by the strong.</i>
<i>That's just how the world works.</i>

4
00:00:17,539 --> 00:00:18,540
15 YEARS EARLIER, BUSAN

5
00:00:18,624 --> 00:00:22,169
Come here! [grunts]
Why'd you bring this thing?

6
00:00:22,252 --> 00:00:25,881
What? Were you gonna
put a bullet in my head? Huh?

7
00:00:25,964 --> 00:00:27,215
[grunts]

8
00:00:27,299 --> 00:00:29,676
A goddamn Jap like you
should know your place.

9
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:33,263
[panting] Your brother's probably off
to report his missing pistol,

10
00:00:33,347 --> 00:00:35,015
but you're the one who stole it!

11
00:00:35,098 --> 00:00:36,266
[both grunting]

12
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:38,352
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

13
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:41,063
You see what happens, you bastard?

14
00:00:41,647 --> 00:00:44,191
Know your damn place, kid. All right?

15
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:45,692
[spits]

16
00:00:45,776 --> 00:00:46,943
[pants]

17
00:00:47,027 --> 00:00:48,362
I'm taking this, by the way.

18
00:00:49,237 --> 00:00:50,614
What a little shit.

19
00:00:52,032 --> 00:00:54,076
-[yells]
-[grunts]

20
00:00:54,159 --> 00:00:55,660
Get the hell off me!

21
00:00:55,744 --> 00:00:58,538
[both grunting]

22
00:01:05,462 --> 00:01:06,463
[both yell]

23
00:01:06,546 --> 00:01:07,839
[gunshot]

24
00:01:11,176 --> 00:01:12,594
[Kihyun] <i>My brother always said,</i>

25
00:01:13,136 --> 00:01:16,765
<i>"If you don't want to get crushed</i>
<i>by your enemies, crush them first."</i>

26
00:01:16,848 --> 00:01:18,016
Where is he?

27
00:01:18,517 --> 00:01:19,893
[breathing heavily]

28
00:01:23,021 --> 00:01:24,398
Give me the gun.

29
00:01:31,613 --> 00:01:33,156
Go home and wait till later.

30
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:35,242
[♪ tense music playing]

31
00:01:36,326 --> 00:01:37,703
[door opens]

32
00:01:48,672 --> 00:01:50,048
[sighs]

33
00:02:16,199 --> 00:02:18,869
[Kihyun] <i>Kitae never asked me</i>
<i>why I killed the guy,</i>

34
00:02:20,162 --> 00:02:22,330
<i>and I never asked</i>
<i>what he did with the body.</i>

35
00:02:22,414 --> 00:02:24,166
<i>An unspoken agreement.</i>

36
00:02:28,712 --> 00:02:31,631
<i>And that day,</i>
<i>the day I thought it was all over,</i>

37
00:02:31,715 --> 00:02:33,091
<i>everything began.</i>

38
00:02:34,009 --> 00:02:35,719
[gunshot echoes]

39
00:02:35,802 --> 00:02:37,304
[♪ theme music playing]

40
00:03:31,858 --> 00:03:34,319
[phone rings]

41
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:37,948
This is Baek Kihyun.

42
00:03:38,031 --> 00:03:39,533
Is Jang back?

43
00:03:44,538 --> 00:03:46,665
Yes. May I help you with something?

44
00:03:47,582 --> 00:03:49,709
<i>He just got his hands</i>
<i>on the slush fund ledger.</i>

45
00:03:50,418 --> 00:03:53,255
<i>Stay sharp, find out exactly</i>
<i>what's going on, and report back to me.</i>

46
00:03:54,047 --> 00:03:55,632
<i>720-1879.</i>

47
00:03:55,715 --> 00:03:58,969
If anything happens, you call me.
Understood?

48
00:03:59,594 --> 00:04:01,596
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

49
00:04:23,410 --> 00:04:24,661
[exhales deeply]

50
00:04:26,913 --> 00:04:28,707
[Geonyoung] <i>If you want</i>
<i>your sister to live</i>

51
00:04:28,790 --> 00:04:31,084
<i>and your niece to have a normal childhood,</i>

52
00:04:32,168 --> 00:04:34,629
<i>you have to ensure you survive first.</i>

53
00:04:56,359 --> 00:04:57,444
[door opens]

54
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,281
-Sir.
-Yeah.

55
00:05:01,364 --> 00:05:02,949
We're ready to move out.

56
00:05:03,033 --> 00:05:05,577
If we arrest Cheon Seokjung,
will you question him yourself

57
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:07,037
or will somebody else do it?

58
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,496
Baek Kihyun will be up to it.

59
00:05:09,331 --> 00:05:10,540
Baek Kihyun's pretty green.

60
00:05:10,624 --> 00:05:11,833
Let's give him a chance.

61
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:16,338
Did you request a warrant for Cheon?
Just tell me, and be honest.

62
00:05:16,421 --> 00:05:17,422
Yes.

63
00:05:18,214 --> 00:05:20,592
-You upset about that?
-What'd you charge him with?

64
00:05:25,472 --> 00:05:28,099
I told you, we're taking him down
for his slush fund!

65
00:05:28,183 --> 00:05:30,185
And what about the whole drug ring?

66
00:05:30,268 --> 00:05:32,729
We're shifting the investigation
to go after the slush fund,

67
00:05:32,812 --> 00:05:34,564
-not the drugs, Miss Oh.
-[Yejin] Sir, come on.

68
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:37,359
Are you sure you want this case
to get political?

69
00:05:37,442 --> 00:05:38,944
-[Jaeho] Ugh, this girl.
-[shouts] "This girl"?

70
00:05:39,027 --> 00:05:41,196
-Don't you dare talk to me like that!
-Colonel Ahn!

71
00:05:42,614 --> 00:05:44,115
Just relax, both of you.

72
00:05:45,825 --> 00:05:47,535
Ahn, get moving. Let's go.

73
00:05:51,039 --> 00:05:52,415
Sir, we're moving out.

74
00:05:54,125 --> 00:05:57,128
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

75
00:05:57,212 --> 00:05:58,421
[door opens]

76
00:06:04,302 --> 00:06:06,388
[Jaeho] When we arrest Cheon Seokjung…

77
00:06:08,181 --> 00:06:09,307
[Yejin sighs]

78
00:06:10,558 --> 00:06:12,936
If you let those politicians in uniform
pull your strings,

79
00:06:13,937 --> 00:06:15,814
they'll stab you in the damn back.

80
00:06:18,692 --> 00:06:21,069
SPECIAL ADVISOR JANG GEONYOUNG

81
00:06:21,152 --> 00:06:22,237
[door closes]

82
00:06:36,918 --> 00:06:38,503
[phone rings]

83
00:06:40,463 --> 00:06:41,464
Yes?

84
00:06:42,215 --> 00:06:44,884
<i>This is Baek Kihyun. Where's my brother?</i>

85
00:06:45,844 --> 00:06:47,178
He's with Chief Cheon.

86
00:06:48,930 --> 00:06:52,142
All right, Cheon is going to be arrested.
Orders came down.

87
00:06:54,561 --> 00:06:56,229
You really think you can handle that?

88
00:06:56,938 --> 00:06:58,356
Oh, it would be my pleasure.

89
00:07:00,942 --> 00:07:03,153
I'll do it, my own way.

90
00:07:03,737 --> 00:07:05,739
[♪ music continues]

91
00:07:10,452 --> 00:07:11,619
[exhales]

92
00:07:13,913 --> 00:07:15,707
-[knocks on door]
-[door opens]

93
00:07:23,298 --> 00:07:25,675
[whispers] They've issued
an arrest warrant for Chief Cheon.

94
00:07:29,763 --> 00:07:32,015
[door opens, closes]

95
00:07:32,098 --> 00:07:33,099
What is it?

96
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:37,437
The JIH has a warrant.
They'll be coming for you soon, sir.

97
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,856
[inhales deeply]

98
00:07:42,609 --> 00:07:44,319
So they're finally doing it.

99
00:07:46,112 --> 00:07:47,530
They're making a move.

100
00:07:48,656 --> 00:07:50,033
Better get going.

101
00:07:56,331 --> 00:07:57,540
Forget it.

102
00:08:00,293 --> 00:08:02,420
It won't solve anything if I run.

103
00:08:05,256 --> 00:08:07,634
I need you to take out Hwang
for good, Kitae.

104
00:08:08,343 --> 00:08:09,928
That's the only way I survive.

105
00:08:12,764 --> 00:08:14,224
Tell me you understand.

106
00:08:15,517 --> 00:08:16,684
Yes, absolutely.

107
00:08:16,768 --> 00:08:17,977
[engine idling]

108
00:08:26,903 --> 00:08:30,198
Go to your hotel, take a hot shower,
and get some good rest.

109
00:08:31,616 --> 00:08:34,786
My investigators will ensure
you get to the airport safely tomorrow.

110
00:08:37,121 --> 00:08:39,541
Let's hope the two of us
never meet in Korea again.

111
00:08:57,976 --> 00:08:59,269
Chief Cheon Seokjung.

112
00:08:59,978 --> 00:09:02,605
I'm Jang Geonyoung.
Nice to finally meet you.

113
00:09:04,274 --> 00:09:05,900
I've always wanted to introduce myself.

114
00:09:06,484 --> 00:09:07,944
It's a big honor to have you visit.

115
00:09:08,862 --> 00:09:09,904
So, shall we?

116
00:09:11,114 --> 00:09:12,115
[Jaeho] Right this way.

117
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:21,958
Get moving, okay?

118
00:09:25,461 --> 00:09:26,671
Choi Yuji.

119
00:09:29,048 --> 00:09:30,133
You did well.

120
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:53,907
[Jaeho]<i> Listen, I want you to handle</i>
<i>the interrogation of Chief Cheon yourself.</i>

121
00:09:54,490 --> 00:09:58,536
<i>This is a direct order from Advisor Jang,</i>
<i>so don't disappoint us.</i>

122
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,830
[both slurping]

123
00:10:06,044 --> 00:10:07,170
[exhales]

124
00:10:08,296 --> 00:10:11,549
Are you sure
that we should use Colonel Baek for this?

125
00:10:12,091 --> 00:10:14,802
-I'm on the fence.
-Uh-huh.

126
00:10:15,929 --> 00:10:17,180
Baek's up to it.

127
00:10:17,931 --> 00:10:20,099
I wanna see what his strategy is.

128
00:10:23,770 --> 00:10:26,314
This book documents
a 70 billion won slush fund,

129
00:10:26,397 --> 00:10:27,690
which you moved to Japan.

130
00:10:29,025 --> 00:10:31,903
Choi Yuji, the head of the Ikeda clan,
already testified.

131
00:10:31,986 --> 00:10:33,363
She managed the fund.

132
00:10:33,446 --> 00:10:35,698
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

133
00:10:35,782 --> 00:10:38,034
What are your ties to the Ikeda family?

134
00:10:41,913 --> 00:10:44,540
How about this.
Where did you get the money?

135
00:10:48,503 --> 00:10:49,629
[on speakers] <i>Chief Cheon.</i>

136
00:10:51,256 --> 00:10:52,840
<i>If you continue to remain silent,</i>

137
00:10:52,924 --> 00:10:56,135
<i>we'll have no choice</i>
<i>but to consider it an admission of guilt.</i>

138
00:11:02,642 --> 00:11:03,643
[sighs]

139
00:11:04,936 --> 00:11:05,937
Do you…

140
00:11:09,482 --> 00:11:11,609
really want me to be honest here?

141
00:11:20,076 --> 00:11:21,619
Just remember…

142
00:11:25,373 --> 00:11:27,250
your brother's not gonna look good.

143
00:11:32,588 --> 00:11:34,007
Bit of a minefield, eh?

144
00:11:34,632 --> 00:11:35,800
[chuckles]

145
00:11:40,138 --> 00:11:42,640
You can pretend, but I know you're lying.

146
00:11:51,691 --> 00:11:52,984
[microphone feedback]

147
00:11:54,319 --> 00:11:55,820
[Geonyoung] <i>Ah, ah.</i>
<i>They can hear me, right?</i>

148
00:11:55,903 --> 00:11:57,655
-[Jaeho] <i>Yeah.</i>
-[Geonyoung clears throat]

149
00:11:58,531 --> 00:11:59,782
Well, Colonel.

150
00:11:59,866 --> 00:12:01,617
<i>I think that's enough for today.</i>

151
00:12:02,201 --> 00:12:03,786
<i>You must be getting tired.</i>

152
00:12:04,495 --> 00:12:05,872
[chuckling]

153
00:12:24,849 --> 00:12:26,059
[electricity buzzes]

154
00:12:31,356 --> 00:12:33,149
[door locks]

155
00:12:42,533 --> 00:12:44,952
[sighing] You gotta be kidding me.

156
00:12:46,746 --> 00:12:48,998
A literal shithole.

157
00:12:51,292 --> 00:12:53,378
[phone ringing]

158
00:12:55,421 --> 00:12:56,589
[sighs]

159
00:13:00,385 --> 00:13:01,677
[Kitae] <i>How's Cheon doing?</i>

160
00:13:02,887 --> 00:13:06,265
He's been keeping his mouth shut,
but he won't be able to hold out.

161
00:13:07,934 --> 00:13:11,020
<i>Once he starts talking, it's all over.</i>
<i>You know that, right?</i>

162
00:13:11,938 --> 00:13:14,565
No, I'm putting an end to it.
He needs to hold out a little longer.

163
00:13:15,608 --> 00:13:17,026
What's your angle now?

164
00:13:17,110 --> 00:13:19,028
<i>You just keep a close eye on him, okay?</i>

165
00:13:19,112 --> 00:13:21,197
Oh, and, where's Choi Yuji?

166
00:13:22,156 --> 00:13:24,158
<i>She was released. She's at a hotel.</i>

167
00:13:24,242 --> 00:13:26,327
<i>She's going back to Japan</i>
<i>on the first flight tomorrow.</i>

168
00:13:26,411 --> 00:13:27,537
Which hotel?

169
00:13:28,079 --> 00:13:31,207
You won't be able to get to her.
The place is crawling with armed guards.

170
00:13:31,290 --> 00:13:33,084
[shouting] I said, which hotel?

171
00:13:33,167 --> 00:13:34,293
[sighs]

172
00:13:36,087 --> 00:13:38,047
<i>Tower Hotel, Room 925.</i>

173
00:13:38,131 --> 00:13:39,841
[phone slams into cradle]

174
00:13:44,595 --> 00:13:46,597
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

175
00:14:16,627 --> 00:14:17,879
Colonel Baek…

176
00:14:25,761 --> 00:14:26,846
You heading home yet?

177
00:14:28,723 --> 00:14:30,641
I have a few more things to do, sir.

178
00:14:32,935 --> 00:14:34,604
Don't push yourself too hard.

179
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:37,231
See you tomorrow.

180
00:14:37,315 --> 00:14:39,317
[♪ music continues]

181
00:14:52,538 --> 00:14:54,665
-[door closes]
-[sighs]

182
00:15:29,825 --> 00:15:32,453
Director Baek,
you're not allowed to see her.

183
00:15:32,954 --> 00:15:34,247
[groans]

184
00:15:34,330 --> 00:15:36,457
[grunting, groaning]

185
00:15:48,344 --> 00:15:49,470
[hammer cocks]

186
00:15:58,479 --> 00:15:59,522
[door closes]

187
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,333
[exhales deeply]

188
00:16:28,759 --> 00:16:29,885
Are you all right?

189
00:16:34,181 --> 00:16:35,433
I'm sorry.

190
00:16:36,434 --> 00:16:37,977
It was my only option.

191
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:44,025
I would've done the same thing.

192
00:16:44,817 --> 00:16:46,235
Don't apologize, please.

193
00:16:51,198 --> 00:16:52,700
What are you going to do now?

194
00:16:54,327 --> 00:16:55,536
I told you already.

195
00:16:56,787 --> 00:16:59,290
I have to see it through.
I've come this far.

196
00:17:06,297 --> 00:17:08,341
We could go to Japan together,
couldn't we?

197
00:17:09,508 --> 00:17:10,509
We could…

198
00:17:11,469 --> 00:17:12,678
just start over.

199
00:17:12,762 --> 00:17:14,805
You know my hands are tied right now.

200
00:17:14,889 --> 00:17:15,890
Kitae.

201
00:17:18,225 --> 00:17:19,643
You might die here.

202
00:17:25,524 --> 00:17:27,026
Go wait for me in Japan.

203
00:17:27,985 --> 00:17:29,528
As soon as I take care of this,

204
00:17:30,863 --> 00:17:32,239
we'll start over, okay?

205
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:37,787
I'm pretty sure that's a goodbye,
isn't it?

206
00:17:44,710 --> 00:17:46,712
[♪ intriguing music playing]

207
00:17:46,796 --> 00:17:48,297
[breathes deeply]

208
00:18:14,865 --> 00:18:17,702
What we had was nice, wasn't it?

209
00:18:20,996 --> 00:18:22,498
It was pretty good.

210
00:18:25,167 --> 00:18:26,544
[Kitae] It was nice.

211
00:18:30,256 --> 00:18:33,300
We'll be able to… meet again, right?

212
00:18:34,719 --> 00:18:35,970
[Kitae] Yes, we will.

213
00:18:44,729 --> 00:18:47,273
I'll see you in Ikaino
for a big bowl of rice soup.

214
00:18:47,773 --> 00:18:49,400
Just like old times.

215
00:18:51,986 --> 00:18:53,738
I need you to promise me…

216
00:18:57,116 --> 00:18:58,659
that you'll stay alive.

217
00:19:02,663 --> 00:19:03,873
I will, I promise.

218
00:19:04,623 --> 00:19:05,791
I'll get to Japan.

219
00:19:19,889 --> 00:19:21,056
Please, Kitae…

220
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:25,102
when that day comes, let's do it right.

221
00:19:25,186 --> 00:19:27,104
Let's not screw up again.

222
00:19:32,777 --> 00:19:34,236
Love is too special.

223
00:19:38,574 --> 00:19:39,742
We won't mess it up.

224
00:19:41,786 --> 00:19:42,870
I promise, Yuji.

225
00:19:53,547 --> 00:19:55,132
ARMY HEADQUARTERS

226
00:19:55,216 --> 00:19:57,676
I'd like to thank all the commanders

227
00:19:57,760 --> 00:19:59,428
for attending this meeting today.

228
00:20:00,638 --> 00:20:01,639
Above all,

229
00:20:01,722 --> 00:20:04,433
I expect you all to make national security
your number one priority.

230
00:20:04,517 --> 00:20:05,518
CHIEF OF STAFF, R.O.K ARMY

231
00:20:05,601 --> 00:20:08,437
Please commit yourself
to the rule of law and order,

232
00:20:08,521 --> 00:20:11,357
and work tirelessly
to regain economic stability.

233
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:13,108
[laughing]

234
00:20:13,192 --> 00:20:15,319
Oh, shoot, sorry about that.

235
00:20:16,070 --> 00:20:17,905
Sorry I'm late. Apologies.

236
00:20:25,704 --> 00:20:28,499
Oh, sorry, General.
Uh, keep talking. [chuckles]

237
00:20:29,124 --> 00:20:30,584
-[exhales loudly]
-Some water, sir?

238
00:20:31,502 --> 00:20:32,545
[Mujin scoffs]

239
00:20:34,046 --> 00:20:36,757
-Very well. If there are no objections…
-[exhales loudly]

240
00:20:36,841 --> 00:20:40,052
…I'd like to ask the head
of the JIH a brief question.

241
00:20:40,135 --> 00:20:42,054
You know, before we proceed further.

242
00:20:43,138 --> 00:20:44,473
Yes, General Jang?

243
00:20:44,557 --> 00:20:46,433
I hear you've been extremely busy.

244
00:20:46,517 --> 00:20:48,310
[chuckles]

245
00:20:48,394 --> 00:20:50,729
Extremely? No, sir. No, I'm just…

246
00:20:50,813 --> 00:20:53,190
I'm just trying to do good work
at the job I've been given.

247
00:20:53,274 --> 00:20:55,025
[chuckles] Is that right?

248
00:20:55,109 --> 00:20:57,361
-Yes.
-Then answer me this.

249
00:20:58,487 --> 00:21:00,447
Did I ever give an order

250
00:21:00,531 --> 00:21:04,493
for you to take over as chair
of the vice ministers' council?

251
00:21:05,619 --> 00:21:08,455
Uh, with martial law in effect,

252
00:21:08,539 --> 00:21:09,999
there seemed to be a lot of confusion

253
00:21:10,082 --> 00:21:12,042
with the jurisdictions
of different ministries,

254
00:21:12,126 --> 00:21:14,128
so I thought it'd be good for the JIH to--

255
00:21:14,211 --> 00:21:18,424
And how do you explain taking Chief Cheon
into punitive custody without permission?

256
00:21:18,507 --> 00:21:22,636
Let me guess, you were
going to report that to us after?

257
00:21:23,470 --> 00:21:25,180
Uh, no, sir, no.

258
00:21:25,973 --> 00:21:28,434
You'll recall my reports
on credible suspicions

259
00:21:28,517 --> 00:21:30,060
of illicit slush fund transactions--

260
00:21:30,144 --> 00:21:32,396
[shouting] Who the damn hell are you?

261
00:21:35,274 --> 00:21:37,443
Hwang Daesik, nice to meet you.

262
00:21:38,944 --> 00:21:40,738
-[officer 1] Sir, Hwang is a good man.
-Do you…

263
00:21:40,821 --> 00:21:43,115
He wouldn't go
behind your back deliberately.

264
00:21:43,198 --> 00:21:44,950
Please be lenient with him.

265
00:21:45,034 --> 00:21:48,495
[officer 2] I agree, sir. General Hwang
has a lot on his plate right now.

266
00:21:48,579 --> 00:21:50,664
I'm sure this was
just a well-meaning blunder.

267
00:21:53,709 --> 00:21:56,587
Is this the duty of an honest soldier?

268
00:21:56,670 --> 00:22:00,591
No, a good soldier knows their role
and they stick to it with integrity!

269
00:22:00,674 --> 00:22:03,302
If you want to sneak around
and play politics with each other,

270
00:22:03,385 --> 00:22:06,764
then please do me a favor
and get out of my sight right now!

271
00:22:16,398 --> 00:22:17,775
General Jang.

272
00:22:19,693 --> 00:22:22,112
My sense of loyalty got the better of me.

273
00:22:23,322 --> 00:22:24,907
I'll try to be careful of that.

274
00:22:25,950 --> 00:22:27,159
"Loyalty"?

275
00:22:27,242 --> 00:22:28,577
That said,

276
00:22:29,495 --> 00:22:31,538
we still intend to carry out

277
00:22:31,622 --> 00:22:35,834
a full investigation
into all who have amassed illicit wealth.

278
00:22:42,341 --> 00:22:45,052
ILLEGAL SLUSH FUND EXPOSED
SIGNS POINT TO KCIA INVOLVEMENT

279
00:22:45,135 --> 00:22:49,390
"Chief of Staff Cheon Seokjung's
Illegal Slush Fund Scheme Exposed.

280
00:22:49,890 --> 00:22:54,478
All Signs Point Directly Toward…
KCIA involvement."

281
00:22:54,561 --> 00:22:56,563
DEPUTY DIRECTOR PYO HAKSU

282
00:22:57,856 --> 00:22:59,650
Yeah, pretty punchy headline.

283
00:23:11,996 --> 00:23:12,997
Director Baek!

284
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:16,125
[anchor] <i>The Joint Investigation</i>
<i>Headquarters announced this morning…</i>

285
00:23:16,208 --> 00:23:19,420
-Hey. What's going on?
<i>-…ledger documenting illegal slush funds</i>

286
00:23:19,503 --> 00:23:22,089
<i>allegedly maintained by</i>
<i>the Chief of Staff, Cheon Seokjung.</i>

287
00:23:22,172 --> 00:23:24,842
<i>The news is sending shock waves</i>
<i>throughout the country…</i>

288
00:23:24,925 --> 00:23:26,468
Did you know about this?

289
00:23:26,552 --> 00:23:29,596
<i>…records of tens of billions of won</i>
<i>in illicit funds, prompting…</i>

290
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:31,974
Oh, fuck, we're screwed! Goddamn…

291
00:23:32,057 --> 00:23:33,726
<i>…the KCIA. According to reports,</i>

292
00:23:33,809 --> 00:23:35,227
<i>-the ledger contains…</i>
-[phone ringing]

293
00:23:35,310 --> 00:23:37,062
<i>…detailed records spanning several years,</i>

294
00:23:37,146 --> 00:23:40,274
<i>documenting how the funds</i>
<i>were accumulated and distributed.</i>

295
00:23:40,357 --> 00:23:43,527
<i>Chief of Staff Cheon Seokjung</i>
<i>is currently being held for questioning</i>

296
00:23:43,610 --> 00:23:45,195
<i>at the Joint Investigation Headquarters,</i>

297
00:23:45,279 --> 00:23:47,781
<i>as government officials</i>
<i>continue to examine</i>

298
00:23:47,865 --> 00:23:51,076
<i>how the slush fund was created</i>
<i>and where the money was spent.</i>

299
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:54,121
<i>The Joint Investigation Headquarters</i>
<i>stated that it will make further…</i>

300
00:23:54,204 --> 00:23:55,205
[Kitae] Yes?

301
00:23:56,915 --> 00:23:58,917
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

302
00:24:07,342 --> 00:24:10,763
That bastard Hwang.
He never reported it to us.

303
00:24:11,805 --> 00:24:14,516
What he's doing is completely outrageous.

304
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:17,978
[Mujin] That son of a bitch must really
think I'll just roll over 'cause of this.

305
00:24:19,146 --> 00:24:22,316
Madam Shin,
what's the best course of action?

306
00:24:22,399 --> 00:24:24,234
What should I do about that asshole?

307
00:24:24,318 --> 00:24:27,654
Well, he must be very pleased
with himself right now.

308
00:24:27,738 --> 00:24:32,076
Sometimes it's good to let a man
enjoy his little victories while he can.

309
00:24:32,659 --> 00:24:34,328
Show some restraint.

310
00:24:34,828 --> 00:24:37,915
Wouldn't you agree, Director Baek?

311
00:24:40,918 --> 00:24:44,338
General, don't worry.
I'll take care of it.

312
00:24:45,172 --> 00:24:46,548
A crisis is an opportunity.

313
00:24:46,632 --> 00:24:48,592
You'll take care of what, exactly?

314
00:24:48,675 --> 00:24:50,052
General Jang.

315
00:24:51,804 --> 00:24:54,556
Be patient. He knows what he's doing.

316
00:24:55,974 --> 00:24:57,768
Baek, be honest.

317
00:24:58,560 --> 00:25:01,146
Is it true? Seventy billion?

318
00:25:01,814 --> 00:25:03,982
[scoffs] No, it's absurd.

319
00:25:04,066 --> 00:25:07,027
It's all lies that Hwang cooked up.

320
00:25:08,904 --> 00:25:10,322
[Mujin groans]

321
00:25:10,405 --> 00:25:12,616
[chuckles] You're right.

322
00:25:13,117 --> 00:25:16,745
Cheon isn't the kind of man
who'd do something like that.

323
00:25:16,829 --> 00:25:21,041
If there's one thing I know about him,
he'd never mess around with money.

324
00:25:21,750 --> 00:25:23,585
Seokjung and I graduated together.

325
00:25:23,669 --> 00:25:25,546
He was ranked first.

326
00:25:27,047 --> 00:25:28,841
And I was ranked second.

327
00:25:29,758 --> 00:25:30,759
[chuckles]

328
00:25:32,719 --> 00:25:37,182
In any case, I'm happy
to entrust this to you, Director.

329
00:25:37,266 --> 00:25:38,267
Yes, sir, I'm on it.

330
00:25:56,076 --> 00:25:57,286
I'll be in touch before long.

331
00:26:10,549 --> 00:26:13,635
Heaven Cloud Pavilion. Do you know it?

332
00:26:15,053 --> 00:26:17,973
Well, it's where Bae Geumji worked.

333
00:26:18,056 --> 00:26:20,017
One of those old courtesan houses.

334
00:26:20,642 --> 00:26:23,645
Hwang Daesik is going to be there
to have some drinks.

335
00:26:23,729 --> 00:26:26,148
[♪ tense music playing]

336
00:26:26,231 --> 00:26:29,067
Weren't you planning
to get this over with and kill him?

337
00:26:31,695 --> 00:26:32,988
You know about that?

338
00:26:35,282 --> 00:26:39,161
You're probably desperate, aren't you?
You're out of options now.

339
00:26:40,913 --> 00:26:41,997
When will he be there?

340
00:26:45,626 --> 00:26:47,085
You broke a girl's heart.

341
00:26:49,421 --> 00:26:52,007
I saw you in my dream last night,
Director Baek.

342
00:26:53,425 --> 00:26:56,678
I remember you were out swimming
in deep blue sea water.

343
00:26:56,762 --> 00:27:00,140
You kept calling out to me,
saying I should join you.

344
00:27:00,224 --> 00:27:01,600
[giggling]

345
00:27:04,519 --> 00:27:08,273
Then earlier today, before my prayer,
I did a cleansing ritual and…

346
00:27:09,107 --> 00:27:10,234
what a surprise…

347
00:27:11,818 --> 00:27:13,695
I saw your face again.

348
00:27:14,446 --> 00:27:16,198
I could see it so clearly.

349
00:27:16,823 --> 00:27:18,200
And guess what?

350
00:27:19,952 --> 00:27:22,412
I could tell you'd broken up with someone.

351
00:27:22,496 --> 00:27:24,164
Your expression was clear.

352
00:27:25,916 --> 00:27:28,251
But there are plenty of women out there.

353
00:27:28,335 --> 00:27:31,838
So bury the memories in your heart,
and abandon past regrets.

354
00:27:34,549 --> 00:27:37,511
It's all right, Kitae.
Somebody new is waiting.

355
00:27:38,178 --> 00:27:39,554
Hmm?

356
00:27:39,638 --> 00:27:40,681
[giggles]

357
00:27:42,975 --> 00:27:45,978
Oh, I'll keep you posted on Hwang Daesik.

358
00:27:53,193 --> 00:27:56,363
HEAVEN CLOUD PAVILION

359
00:28:16,508 --> 00:28:18,093
[Kihun] It's at Heaven Cloud Pavilion.

360
00:28:18,176 --> 00:28:21,096
I confirmed the reservation
under Colonel Ahn's name, sir.

361
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:22,931
It's for the 13th?

362
00:28:24,224 --> 00:28:25,308
That's right.

363
00:28:25,392 --> 00:28:27,352
Get some men you trust,
make sure they're ready.

364
00:28:27,436 --> 00:28:28,895
Pyo should be left out of this.

365
00:28:28,979 --> 00:28:30,272
Yes, sir. I'm on it.

366
00:28:30,355 --> 00:28:31,606
[knocks on door]

367
00:28:31,690 --> 00:28:32,983
[door opens]

368
00:28:48,540 --> 00:28:49,875
[sighs loudly]

369
00:28:51,126 --> 00:28:52,627
I did my research.

370
00:28:52,711 --> 00:28:54,254
That guy Jang Geonyoung?

371
00:28:54,337 --> 00:28:57,716
I tried digging deep,
and it brought up absolutely nothing.

372
00:28:59,968 --> 00:29:01,344
Nobody's close to the guy.

373
00:29:02,512 --> 00:29:05,182
He's like a deserted island. All alone.

374
00:29:06,933 --> 00:29:08,310
[chuckles]

375
00:29:16,026 --> 00:29:17,235
Uh, so…

376
00:29:18,278 --> 00:29:19,446
Sorry about that.

377
00:29:20,739 --> 00:29:22,532
Anyway, the bottom line is…

378
00:29:23,533 --> 00:29:28,121
[exhales sharply] …there is someone
that might be close enough to him.

379
00:29:28,205 --> 00:29:30,207
Oh Yejin, the female prosecutor.

380
00:29:32,709 --> 00:29:33,794
Not his younger sister?

381
00:29:35,045 --> 00:29:38,173
Well, she still lives alone,
no close friends,

382
00:29:39,758 --> 00:29:41,343
no guitar anymore.

383
00:29:42,594 --> 00:29:44,221
She works at the factory still,

384
00:29:44,304 --> 00:29:46,598
but no matter how I look,
there's nothing we can pin on her.

385
00:29:46,681 --> 00:29:48,225
One thing's clear about Jang, though.

386
00:29:49,518 --> 00:29:51,978
He's spent nine years
waiting for an opportunity.

387
00:29:54,231 --> 00:29:55,690
Just to bring you down.

388
00:29:55,774 --> 00:29:56,858
[Kitae scoffs]

389
00:29:57,484 --> 00:29:58,985
[chuckles]

390
00:30:01,071 --> 00:30:02,364
You can go.

391
00:30:16,670 --> 00:30:18,004
Sir, I apologize.

392
00:30:27,347 --> 00:30:30,183
Pyo Haksu. You find anything yet?

393
00:30:30,934 --> 00:30:34,271
Nothing that suggests he's been in contact
with the JIH up to this point.

394
00:30:36,273 --> 00:30:37,899
I'll continue to monitor him.

395
00:30:40,902 --> 00:30:42,779
What made you want to see me again?

396
00:30:43,780 --> 00:30:45,657
The two of us
don't exactly have a cordial,

397
00:30:45,740 --> 00:30:47,701
coffee-house kind of relationship.

398
00:30:47,784 --> 00:30:49,452
[♪ gentle music playing on speakers]

399
00:30:50,162 --> 00:30:52,205
I suppose you shouldn't have come, then.

400
00:30:52,289 --> 00:30:53,290
What?

401
00:30:55,083 --> 00:30:56,293
Wow, that's bitter.

402
00:30:57,669 --> 00:31:00,255
I'm sure you came
because you got worried, right?

403
00:31:01,298 --> 00:31:03,466
Cheon Seokjung's picture
is on the front page,

404
00:31:03,550 --> 00:31:04,759
accusations are flying,

405
00:31:05,677 --> 00:31:07,554
and your brother won't tell you anything.

406
00:31:07,637 --> 00:31:09,181
You're completely in the dark.

407
00:31:10,932 --> 00:31:12,184
I know you're anxious.

408
00:31:12,726 --> 00:31:13,727
Hey.

409
00:31:13,810 --> 00:31:16,563
Just spit out what you came to say.

410
00:31:17,439 --> 00:31:18,440
All right.

411
00:31:21,443 --> 00:31:22,444
Park Changbae.

412
00:31:23,069 --> 00:31:24,154
Where is he?

413
00:31:27,407 --> 00:31:30,076
We've been looking everywhere
and still have no clue.

414
00:31:31,161 --> 00:31:33,705
We don't know if he's dead or alive.

415
00:31:34,456 --> 00:31:36,583
You haven't been able
to reach him either, have you?

416
00:31:37,876 --> 00:31:39,002
[sighs]

417
00:31:39,085 --> 00:31:42,797
My bet is your brother made him
so terrified, he fled the country.

418
00:31:45,300 --> 00:31:46,343
Then again,

419
00:31:47,552 --> 00:31:50,096
Kang Daeil wound up dead,
he wouldn't want the same fate.

420
00:31:51,431 --> 00:31:54,893
You little shit!
Watch your damn mouth, you bitch.

421
00:31:54,976 --> 00:31:58,521
Did you forget what happens
when you challenge my brother?

422
00:32:00,565 --> 00:32:01,983
Oh, of course not.

423
00:32:02,609 --> 00:32:05,612
I'm well aware
of what Director Baek Kitae can do.

424
00:32:06,446 --> 00:32:09,783
And I know exactly
who killed Kang Daeil, too.

425
00:32:15,413 --> 00:32:18,583
That's right. It wasn't suicide.

426
00:32:21,086 --> 00:32:22,212
It was him.

427
00:32:22,837 --> 00:32:25,715
Your own brother took him out. You get it?

428
00:32:27,342 --> 00:32:28,760
[gasps]

429
00:32:30,762 --> 00:32:32,180
[Yejin] Oh, man.

430
00:32:36,434 --> 00:32:38,436
[breathing shakily]

431
00:32:48,947 --> 00:32:51,700
Hi, Minju. It's Uncle Kihyun.
Is your mom around?

432
00:32:54,619 --> 00:32:55,912
Where did she go?

433
00:32:55,996 --> 00:32:58,206
-[typewriter keys clacking]
-[phone ringing]

434
00:33:03,253 --> 00:33:05,755
Please make sure
that your mother calls me, all right?

435
00:33:06,506 --> 00:33:08,133
Mm-hmm. Mmm.

436
00:33:24,232 --> 00:33:26,067
-I won't be gone long.
-Yes, sir.

437
00:33:29,612 --> 00:33:30,989
Anything happen while I was gone?

438
00:33:32,073 --> 00:33:33,616
Uh, Miss Oh.

439
00:33:33,700 --> 00:33:36,661
Mr. Jang. He wants to speak with you.

440
00:33:39,998 --> 00:33:41,374
[Yejin sighs]

441
00:33:47,255 --> 00:33:48,423
[knocks on door]

442
00:33:49,049 --> 00:33:50,300
Yeah?

443
00:33:51,384 --> 00:33:52,635
You wanted me, sir?

444
00:33:54,137 --> 00:33:55,847
Well, you've been gone a lot.

445
00:33:56,806 --> 00:33:58,141
Come take a seat.

446
00:34:07,859 --> 00:34:11,780
These are records of Ikeda Yuji

447
00:34:11,863 --> 00:34:14,032
laundering Cheon's slush funds in Japan.

448
00:34:14,115 --> 00:34:15,116
Take a look.

449
00:34:16,076 --> 00:34:17,369
[grunts]

450
00:34:21,289 --> 00:34:23,458
So where were you today anyway?

451
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:27,796
Baek Soyeong met me for coffee.

452
00:34:28,671 --> 00:34:30,465
Okay, why did you meet with her, then?

453
00:34:33,176 --> 00:34:36,012
Because of a dealer named Park Changbae
who works for her.

454
00:34:36,096 --> 00:34:39,641
He was pushing meth in Busan,
but he suddenly vanished, so…

455
00:34:40,475 --> 00:34:42,143
I met with her briefly. Big deal.

456
00:34:42,227 --> 00:34:44,145
I told you to hold off for now.

457
00:34:45,563 --> 00:34:46,981
[sighs]

458
00:34:48,274 --> 00:34:49,984
I'm not gonna do that, sir.

459
00:34:51,277 --> 00:34:53,822
Want me to just send you back
to Busan, Yejin?

460
00:34:57,033 --> 00:34:59,411
The reason I'm here
is to bust drug dealers.

461
00:35:01,579 --> 00:35:04,124
I honestly don't give a damn
about the slush fund.

462
00:35:04,207 --> 00:35:07,961
A drug dealer should go down for drugs.
And that includes Baek Kitae.

463
00:35:08,044 --> 00:35:10,213
He belongs in prison,
and until I catch the guy,

464
00:35:10,296 --> 00:35:11,631
I'm not going back, all right?

465
00:35:11,715 --> 00:35:13,675
The money he brought in
from his meth empire

466
00:35:13,758 --> 00:35:15,176
is in the slush fund!

467
00:35:15,260 --> 00:35:18,930
Then answer me. Why?
Why drop the drug charges?

468
00:35:19,013 --> 00:35:21,015
[♪ tense music playing]

469
00:35:22,058 --> 00:35:23,768
What about this don't you get?

470
00:35:24,310 --> 00:35:25,353
[Yejin scoffs]

471
00:35:26,229 --> 00:35:27,480
You listen to me.

472
00:35:29,107 --> 00:35:32,235
You've really been confusing
the shit out of me lately.

473
00:35:33,069 --> 00:35:35,905
Are you actually trying to
bring down a drug lord,

474
00:35:36,406 --> 00:35:40,326
or are you just backing military trash
so you can take power later on?

475
00:35:42,078 --> 00:35:43,121
So tell me…

476
00:35:45,498 --> 00:35:47,751
what exactly is your real objective here?

477
00:36:26,331 --> 00:36:27,791
[Minju crying faintly]

478
00:36:38,843 --> 00:36:40,929
Minju. Minju? Hey, Minju.

479
00:36:42,180 --> 00:36:43,348
Are you all right?

480
00:36:44,265 --> 00:36:45,683
-Uncle Kihyun.
-Mm-hmm?

481
00:36:51,272 --> 00:36:53,691
-[sobbing]
-Ah, shit.

482
00:36:53,775 --> 00:36:56,027
[hurried footsteps]

483
00:36:59,906 --> 00:37:02,283
[gasps] Soyeong. Soyeong. Hey.

484
00:37:02,367 --> 00:37:04,160
[Soyeong breathing shakily]

485
00:37:04,244 --> 00:37:07,163
Soyeong. Hey, what's wrong? Huh?

486
00:37:07,247 --> 00:37:08,331
What is it?

487
00:37:10,333 --> 00:37:12,252
[screaming]

488
00:37:12,335 --> 00:37:13,586
[Kihyun] Hey!

489
00:37:13,670 --> 00:37:15,421
[continues screaming]

490
00:37:21,636 --> 00:37:22,720
[glass shatters]

491
00:37:23,388 --> 00:37:26,057
-Get away!
-Soyeong! Soyeong!

492
00:37:26,140 --> 00:37:28,268
-[continues screaming]
-[object smashes]

493
00:37:29,519 --> 00:37:31,479
[Soyeong] Get away from me!

494
00:37:31,563 --> 00:37:34,816
[screaming] No, no! Get away!

495
00:37:34,899 --> 00:37:36,317
It's me! Soyeong!

496
00:37:36,401 --> 00:37:39,404
Hey! It's me, Kihyun. It's Kihyun.

497
00:37:40,280 --> 00:37:42,031
Yeah. [breathing heavily]

498
00:37:44,325 --> 00:37:45,869
[object thuds]

499
00:37:45,952 --> 00:37:47,245
It's me. It's me.

500
00:37:47,328 --> 00:37:50,039
-[breathing heavily]
-[Soyeong breathing shakily]

501
00:37:56,087 --> 00:37:57,714
Da… Daeil.

502
00:37:59,924 --> 00:38:01,843
[sobbing]

503
00:38:03,636 --> 00:38:05,263
I'm sorry.

504
00:38:05,346 --> 00:38:07,348
[♪ somber music playing]

505
00:38:08,850 --> 00:38:10,393
[sobbing] I'm so sorry.

506
00:38:11,352 --> 00:38:12,478
I'm sorry.

507
00:38:15,231 --> 00:38:16,900
-I'm sorry.
-[breathing heavily]

508
00:38:16,983 --> 00:38:18,651
[sobbing]

509
00:38:21,613 --> 00:38:23,573
I'm sorry.

510
00:38:23,656 --> 00:38:24,824
You're all right, hey.

511
00:38:25,617 --> 00:38:26,826
It's okay.

512
00:38:26,910 --> 00:38:29,370
-It's okay.
-I'm so sorry.

513
00:38:29,454 --> 00:38:31,456
[crying, sobbing]

514
00:38:35,293 --> 00:38:37,503
-Minju…
-Hey, Minju's all right. Minju's fine.

515
00:38:37,587 --> 00:38:39,297
-Minju.
-She's fine, okay?

516
00:38:39,380 --> 00:38:40,423
Minju.

517
00:38:40,506 --> 00:38:43,301
-Minju. Dad's here! Don't be scared!
-[grunting]

518
00:38:44,010 --> 00:38:45,386
-Minju, Dad's here!
-[grunting] Hey, no…

519
00:38:45,470 --> 00:38:46,846
-No, stop, Soyeong.
-Hey, Minju!

520
00:38:46,930 --> 00:38:48,556
-Minju! [screams]
-That's enough.

521
00:38:48,640 --> 00:38:50,433
-Soyeong, no!
-Minju!

522
00:38:50,516 --> 00:38:53,269
Minju! [gasping, screaming]

523
00:39:05,490 --> 00:39:08,534
HANGUK UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

524
00:39:08,618 --> 00:39:10,954
[Kitae breathing heavily]

525
00:39:35,603 --> 00:39:36,854
[exhales deeply]

526
00:39:44,821 --> 00:39:47,031
Did you know Soyeong was like this?

527
00:39:47,782 --> 00:39:48,992
That it was this bad?

528
00:39:54,539 --> 00:39:56,624
If I had, I wouldn't have left her alone.

529
00:39:59,460 --> 00:40:01,295
She'll be fine once she gets treatment.

530
00:40:01,379 --> 00:40:03,381
I'm going to do
everything I can to help her.

531
00:40:06,009 --> 00:40:07,760
Are you capable of regret?

532
00:40:10,096 --> 00:40:11,097
What?

533
00:40:12,056 --> 00:40:13,391
Do you ever regret…

534
00:40:15,268 --> 00:40:16,769
the way you've lived your life?

535
00:40:16,853 --> 00:40:18,062
[scoffs]

536
00:40:27,405 --> 00:40:28,489
[scoffs]

537
00:40:32,326 --> 00:40:33,911
What the hell did you just say?

538
00:40:34,746 --> 00:40:37,540
Who do you think put food on your table
all these years?

539
00:40:38,583 --> 00:40:41,210
I was the one earning the money
that fed and clothed you.

540
00:40:43,504 --> 00:40:45,798
I put you through the Military Academy.

541
00:40:47,216 --> 00:40:48,801
You've kept your mouth shut all this time,

542
00:40:48,885 --> 00:40:51,095
and suddenly you've got
a pang of conscience?

543
00:40:51,637 --> 00:40:52,889
And did you notice?

544
00:40:52,972 --> 00:40:56,476
You didn't even realize
what was going on with your own sister!

545
00:40:57,560 --> 00:40:59,353
Just carry on and forget it!

546
00:40:59,437 --> 00:41:01,147
While I take care of everything!

547
00:41:01,230 --> 00:41:02,607
Don't say that!

548
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:07,904
You have got to stop pretending
to be responsible for everything.

549
00:41:07,987 --> 00:41:10,031
Soyeong and I always listened to you.

550
00:41:10,114 --> 00:41:12,450
We spent our whole lives
doing your bidding.

551
00:41:14,077 --> 00:41:16,496
If I had known you were gonna
end up like this,

552
00:41:16,579 --> 00:41:18,831
I would never have lived that way.

553
00:41:21,125 --> 00:41:23,461
Sure, you built a drug ring just for us.

554
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:28,716
Not cause of your bottomless,
all-consuming ambition.

555
00:41:34,889 --> 00:41:36,891
[grunting]

556
00:41:45,942 --> 00:41:47,527
How dare you, you little shit.

557
00:41:47,610 --> 00:41:49,737
[both breathing heavily]

558
00:41:57,078 --> 00:41:58,329
[Kitae exhales sharply]

559
00:42:12,135 --> 00:42:14,095
This is exactly what you did back then.

560
00:42:15,805 --> 00:42:18,015
You never asked about the gun I stole…

561
00:42:20,935 --> 00:42:23,187
or why I shot him in the first place.

562
00:42:24,730 --> 00:42:27,400
Whether it was right or wrong.

563
00:42:30,278 --> 00:42:32,697
You never once said
a single word about it.

564
00:42:35,324 --> 00:42:37,618
Everything went bad from then on.

565
00:42:37,702 --> 00:42:39,078
[♪ somber music playing]

566
00:42:50,882 --> 00:42:53,384
If you were really that unhappy
about me saving your life,

567
00:42:53,467 --> 00:42:54,802
you could've said so.

568
00:42:55,386 --> 00:42:57,388
From now on, live how you want.

569
00:43:22,872 --> 00:43:26,042
Chief Cheon, I hope you slept a little.

570
00:43:28,294 --> 00:43:30,046
It's not a five-course dinner,

571
00:43:30,713 --> 00:43:32,757
but I thought I'd bring you
something to eat.

572
00:43:32,840 --> 00:43:33,841
Here.

573
00:43:35,051 --> 00:43:37,220
You should have a little soju too.

574
00:43:43,351 --> 00:43:44,644
[Seokjung groans softly]

575
00:43:46,145 --> 00:43:47,396
[Geonyoung sighs]

576
00:43:49,398 --> 00:43:50,775
[scoffs]

577
00:44:10,002 --> 00:44:11,170
[exhales]

578
00:44:11,254 --> 00:44:14,257
CHIEF OF STAFF TO THE PRESIDENT
CHEON'S SLUSH FUND SCANDAL

579
00:44:17,134 --> 00:44:18,261
So, that money.

580
00:44:19,679 --> 00:44:21,681
What were you planning to do with it?

581
00:44:21,764 --> 00:44:24,934
And it was all from drugs, right?
All 70 billion?

582
00:44:26,143 --> 00:44:29,605
Looks like you were planning to use it
to make yourself president.

583
00:44:30,231 --> 00:44:31,232
Wait a second.

584
00:44:32,233 --> 00:44:34,151
If you'd been able to pull that off,

585
00:44:34,235 --> 00:44:37,154
meth would've become
our biggest national industry.

586
00:44:37,238 --> 00:44:39,073
[laughing]

587
00:44:43,119 --> 00:44:45,162
It was Baek Kitae's idea though, right?

588
00:44:51,210 --> 00:44:55,006
Man, you're really desperate
to catch Baek Kitae, aren't you?

589
00:44:58,926 --> 00:45:01,053
You must still be holding a grudge…

590
00:45:02,847 --> 00:45:05,349
over what he did to you. [chuckles]

591
00:45:06,976 --> 00:45:08,394
Come on, you and Kitae?

592
00:45:10,313 --> 00:45:13,316
When it really comes down to it,
you guys are two of a kind,

593
00:45:14,483 --> 00:45:15,484
yeah?

594
00:45:20,156 --> 00:45:21,240
[chuckles]

595
00:45:29,957 --> 00:45:31,292
[exhales loudly]

596
00:45:33,210 --> 00:45:34,420
Hmm.

597
00:45:37,923 --> 00:45:39,884
Seems like talking's unproductive.

598
00:45:40,426 --> 00:45:42,053
[laughs]

599
00:45:44,680 --> 00:45:47,266
-What, am I gonna be tortured next?
-Torture?

600
00:45:48,267 --> 00:45:49,852
That's always been your specialty.

601
00:45:50,394 --> 00:45:52,396
Ya know, waterboarding and all that?

602
00:45:52,480 --> 00:45:55,191
Killed plenty of guys like that
back in the day, didn't you?

603
00:45:56,233 --> 00:45:59,195
All the techniques you used
back then are still around.

604
00:46:00,363 --> 00:46:03,532
Your methods are being carried on
by the next generation.

605
00:46:06,911 --> 00:46:08,454
We're ready.

606
00:46:08,537 --> 00:46:10,122
[♪ tense music playing]

607
00:46:12,041 --> 00:46:13,376
Clothes off.

608
00:46:14,085 --> 00:46:15,753
[grunting]

609
00:46:22,051 --> 00:46:23,094
[water bubbling]

610
00:46:25,304 --> 00:46:27,056
[grunting]

611
00:46:32,478 --> 00:46:33,854
[gasping]

612
00:46:34,939 --> 00:46:36,107
[water bubbling]

613
00:46:39,860 --> 00:46:42,154
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

614
00:46:42,238 --> 00:46:45,741
I think the madam here
knows Hwang Daesik pretty well by now.

615
00:46:46,242 --> 00:46:48,869
Whenever he plans to meet someone
discreetly, this is where he brings them.

616
00:46:48,953 --> 00:46:49,954
HEAVEN CLOUD PAVILION

617
00:46:52,915 --> 00:46:55,042
<i>From what I've gathered,</i>
<i>he goes there regularly,</i>

618
00:46:55,126 --> 00:46:56,377
<i>at least once a month.</i>

619
00:46:56,460 --> 00:46:59,755
<i>He usually arrives in the evening</i>
<i>and stays for around three hours.</i>

620
00:47:00,381 --> 00:47:03,217
This house is about a hundred meters
from Heaven Cloud Pavilion,

621
00:47:03,300 --> 00:47:05,594
<i>so we'll be using it</i>
<i>as our base of operations.</i>

622
00:47:06,345 --> 00:47:09,557
<i>The owner and his family</i>
<i>have already been sent out of town.</i>

623
00:47:15,146 --> 00:47:16,230
This is C-4.

624
00:47:16,313 --> 00:47:18,816
They used it for breaching
and demolition during the Vietnam War.

625
00:47:21,444 --> 00:47:23,279
<i>It has a lethal radius of 50 meters,</i>

626
00:47:24,071 --> 00:47:26,949
<i>and about the same explosive power</i>
<i>as six hand grenades.</i>

627
00:47:27,032 --> 00:47:29,410
As you can see, it's fitted with a timer.

628
00:47:30,244 --> 00:47:33,289
Once we activate the detonator
remotely from the operations base,

629
00:47:34,457 --> 00:47:36,709
<i>-it'll start counting down.</i>
-[ticking]

630
00:47:37,334 --> 00:47:40,421
[Kihun] Now, if you cut this red wire,
the countdown will stop.

631
00:47:40,504 --> 00:47:42,214
It has to be the red wire.

632
00:47:42,298 --> 00:47:45,342
If you cut the blue one by mistake,
it'll go off immediately.

633
00:47:47,595 --> 00:47:48,929
All the pieces are in place.

634
00:47:50,264 --> 00:47:51,265
Director.

635
00:47:53,142 --> 00:47:54,310
Shall we do this?

636
00:48:01,150 --> 00:48:02,485
[lighter flicks open]

637
00:48:48,572 --> 00:48:49,573
Start it.

638
00:48:58,123 --> 00:48:59,833
[ticking]

639
00:48:59,917 --> 00:49:03,796
Uh, I know that everyone's been busy
serving the country,

640
00:49:03,879 --> 00:49:05,756
so I appreciate you making the time.

641
00:49:06,382 --> 00:49:08,884
In return, I can promise you one thing…

642
00:49:08,968 --> 00:49:12,012
'cause you're my friends,
you're gonna be treated right today!

643
00:49:12,096 --> 00:49:13,889
[all laughing]

644
00:49:14,765 --> 00:49:16,934
All right, with that in mind…

645
00:49:17,017 --> 00:49:18,644
[groans]

646
00:49:19,812 --> 00:49:21,063
Raise a glass.

647
00:49:23,649 --> 00:49:25,985
-We are…
-[all] We are one!

648
00:49:30,614 --> 00:49:33,659
[exhales loudly] Huh?

649
00:49:54,722 --> 00:49:57,683
I didn't gather you all here
just for fun today.

650
00:49:57,766 --> 00:50:02,229
I also wanted to introduce you
to the newest JIH member.

651
00:50:04,440 --> 00:50:07,234
This man is, well, how should I put this…

652
00:50:07,860 --> 00:50:11,739
He's the brains
behind our latest operation. [chuckles]

653
00:50:12,489 --> 00:50:14,241
Our very own Zhuge Liang.

654
00:50:14,325 --> 00:50:17,536
Let's welcome our advisor, Jang Geonyoung.

655
00:50:28,172 --> 00:50:29,423
Nice to meet everybody.

656
00:50:30,341 --> 00:50:32,593
Given the rise of instability and crime,

657
00:50:32,676 --> 00:50:36,347
I plan to do my absolute best
for the Joint Investigation Headquarters,

658
00:50:36,430 --> 00:50:39,433
rooting out corruption,
abuses of government power,

659
00:50:39,516 --> 00:50:41,602
and money laundering
taking place overseas.

660
00:50:42,561 --> 00:50:43,896
I appreciate your support.

661
00:50:44,396 --> 00:50:45,397
Let's hear it for him.

662
00:50:47,316 --> 00:50:49,026
[ticking]

663
00:50:51,987 --> 00:50:53,530
Wait a minute, isn't that…

664
00:50:54,531 --> 00:50:55,532
Director.

665
00:50:57,326 --> 00:50:58,619
Isn't that your brother?

666
00:50:59,411 --> 00:51:00,412
What did you say?

667
00:51:33,904 --> 00:51:35,406
[breath trembles]

668
00:51:40,577 --> 00:51:41,954
Sir!

669
00:51:43,664 --> 00:51:46,417
I got into a minor accident on my way.
Sorry I'm late.

670
00:51:47,000 --> 00:51:49,586
Oh, no. You're not hurt, are you?

671
00:51:49,670 --> 00:51:51,004
No, sir. I'm fine.

672
00:51:51,088 --> 00:51:53,424
I see you've got good looks
and spirit, too.

673
00:51:53,507 --> 00:51:54,508
Tell me your name?

674
00:51:54,591 --> 00:51:56,468
Lieutenant Colonel Baek Kihyun, sir!

675
00:51:56,552 --> 00:51:59,012
All right. Happy to have you here.

676
00:51:59,096 --> 00:52:00,097
Much appreciated.

677
00:52:00,180 --> 00:52:02,891
Colonel Baek, take a seat down there.

678
00:52:02,975 --> 00:52:03,976
Yes, of course.

679
00:52:07,229 --> 00:52:08,230
Thank you.

680
00:52:19,158 --> 00:52:21,160
[ticking]

681
00:52:27,458 --> 00:52:29,084
[breath trembling]

682
00:52:31,170 --> 00:52:34,006
This time, how about
we let Colonel Baek take the lead.

683
00:52:34,089 --> 00:52:36,425
Just give us a nice, proud "We are."

684
00:52:37,301 --> 00:52:38,302
We are!

685
00:52:38,927 --> 00:52:40,095
[all] We are one!

686
00:52:43,098 --> 00:52:45,768
[officer grunts, laughs]

687
00:52:52,107 --> 00:52:54,902
-[Hwang] What's this?
-Hey, not yet. What's going on?

688
00:52:55,486 --> 00:52:57,279
I don't believe I called for you.

689
00:52:57,362 --> 00:53:00,866
Well, General,
I couldn't help myself. [giggles]

690
00:53:00,949 --> 00:53:02,618
I called for them, sir.

691
00:53:19,009 --> 00:53:21,595
[ticking]

692
00:53:24,431 --> 00:53:26,433
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

